WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.101 --> 00:00:09.489
Jason walked slowly into the kitchen behind his friends.

2
00:00:09.490 --> 00:00:14.530
"We're making oven-fried chicken today," Chef said.

3
00:00:14.531 --> 00:00:20.347
"Yum! Could we have a picnic outside?" Izzie said.

4
00:00:20.348 --> 00:00:26.737
"Okay. Just behave yourselves and pay attention," Chef said sternly.

5
00:00:26.738 --> 00:00:31.078
Everyone cheered except for Jason.

6
00:00:31.079 --> 00:00:35.149
He crossed his arms and frowned.

7
00:00:35.150 --> 00:00:42.629
"What's wrong? You're as grumpy as Chef!" Bobby said.

8
00:00:42.630 --> 00:00:46.999
"I heard that, Bobby!" Chef snapped.

9
00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:50.392
"Sorry, Chef," Bobby said.

10
00:00:50.393 --> 00:00:53.612
"I'll do the first step."

11
00:00:53.613 --> 00:00:57.353
Bobby put a half cup of butter in a pan.

12
00:00:57.354 --> 00:01:00.823
Chef turned on the oven.

13
00:01:00.824 --> 00:01:04.626
He put the pan inside to melt the butter.

14
00:01:04.627 --> 00:01:08.871
"Next we'll coat the chicken in flour," Chef said.

15
00:01:08.872 --> 00:01:13.766
Nina measured two-thirds cup of flour into a bowl.

16
00:01:13.767 --> 00:01:17.962
The kids took turns picking up the chicken with tongs.

17
00:01:17.963 --> 00:01:22.292
They coated each piece with flour.

18
00:01:22.293 --> 00:01:25.865
"Now comes the fun part," Chef said.

19
00:01:25.866 --> 00:01:29.687
"We need cracker crumbs."

20
00:01:29.688 --> 00:01:35.741
He gave each kid a plastic bag of crackers. "Crush them!"

21
00:01:35.742 --> 00:01:40.068
Nina used a rolling pin to crush the crackers.

22
00:01:40.069 --> 00:01:43.850
Izzie found a mallet.

23
00:01:43.851 --> 00:01:48.332
Bobby pounded his bag on the counter with his fist.

24
00:01:48.333 --> 00:01:51.106
Jason just watched everyone.

25
00:01:51.107 --> 00:01:56.377
"Jason, why aren't you following directions?" Chef asked.

26
00:01:56.378 --> 00:02:01.307
"I don't feel like cooking today," Jason said.

27
00:02:01.308 --> 00:02:05.051
"But you love cooking!" Nina said.

28
00:02:05.052 --> 00:02:13.637
"Not anymore." Jason sighed and handed his bag to Bobby.

29
00:02:13.638 --> 00:02:17.495
The kids poured the cracker crumbs into a bowl.

30
00:02:17.496 --> 00:02:19.915
Izzie looked at the screen.

31
00:02:19.916 --> 00:02:23.771
"We need four eggs. I'll crack two!"

32
00:02:23.772 --> 00:02:32.134
"I'll crack the other two," Nina said.

33
00:02:32.135 --> 00:02:37.465
Bobby added salt and paprika to the bowl of eggs.

34
00:02:37.466 --> 00:02:40.961
"Jason, add the lemon juice," Chef said.

35
00:02:40.962 --> 00:02:45.297
Jason shrugged. "Okay."

36
00:02:45.298 --> 00:02:51.764
He put four tablespoons of lemon juice in the bowl.

37
00:02:51.765 --> 00:02:55.402
Bobby whisked the ingredients together.

38
00:02:55.403 --> 00:02:58.809
"Now dip the chicken pieces in the egg mixture.

39
00:02:58.810 --> 00:03:03.448
Then coat them in the crumbs," Chef said.

40
00:03:03.449 --> 00:03:07.481
The kids followed his directions.

41
00:03:07.482 --> 00:03:11.802
"We'll bake the pieces for 45 minutes," Chef said.

42
00:03:11.803 --> 00:03:21.113
"We'll turn them over halfway through."

43
00:03:21.114 --> 00:03:23.902
The kids got busy cleaning.

44
00:03:23.903 --> 00:03:28.028
Bobby wiped the counters while Izzie swept the floor.

45
00:03:28.029 --> 00:03:31.659
Jason and Nina washed dishes.

46
00:03:31.660 --> 00:03:36.124
"Jason, why don't you like to cook anymore?" Chef asked.

47
00:03:36.125 --> 00:03:39.015
"You're an excellent junior chef."

48
00:03:39.016 --> 00:03:44.517
Jason sighed. "Mom and I cook together all the time.

49
00:03:44.518 --> 00:03:48.907
But when it's just Dad and me, he's always tired after work.

50
00:03:48.908 --> 00:03:52.224
So we get takeout."

51
00:03:52.225 --> 00:03:58.117
Bobby rubbed his stomach. "Mmm! Takeout!"

52
00:03:58.118 --> 00:04:03.712
"It's good but it's usually not that healthy," Izzie said.

53
00:04:03.713 --> 00:04:08.952
"I wish Dad and I could make meals together," Jason said.

54
00:04:08.953 --> 00:04:13.624
"Have you told your dad you want to cook?" Nina asked.

55
00:04:13.625 --> 00:04:16.517
"Sure," Jason said.

56
00:04:16.518 --> 00:04:19.589
"But we never have the ingredients I need.

57
00:04:19.590 --> 00:04:23.083
Dad doesn't have time for shopping either."

58
00:04:23.084 --> 00:04:28.346
"When my mom is busy, she has groceries delivered," Izzie said.

59
00:04:28.347 --> 00:04:33.015
"Huh," Jason said, thinking.

60
00:04:33.016 --> 00:04:36.432
Soon the chicken was ready.

61
00:04:36.433 --> 00:04:41.353
Chef placed it on a platter.

62
00:04:41.354 --> 00:04:45.773
He took out some rolls and a salad.

63
00:04:45.774 --> 00:04:51.998
They carried everything to the picnic table outside.

64
00:04:51.999 --> 00:04:54.407
Jason looked at the food.

65
00:04:54.408 --> 00:04:57.070
"I could make this dinner at home.

66
00:04:57.071 --> 00:05:01.670
I'll ask Dad to get groceries delivered, and we'll cook together."

67
00:05:01.671 --> 00:05:04.952
His friends and Chef clapped.

68
00:05:04.953 --> 00:05:11.311
Jason grinned. "What are we cooking next, Chef?"

